%% @version 1.0.0
%% @date 2026-07-24
%% @type sequence
%% @level system
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Client as Pipeline Component
    participant UHC as UnifiedHTTPClient
    participant RateLimiter as Rate Limiter
    participant CircuitBreaker as Circuit Breaker
    participant RetryPolicy as Retry Policy
    participant HTTP as HTTP Client
    participant Server as External API Server
    participant Metrics as Metrics/Tracing
    participant Logger as Structured Logger

    Note over Client, Logger: HTTP Request/Response Flow (ADR-032)

    %% Initial Request
    Client->>UHC: Make HTTP request (method, url, params)
    UHC->>Metrics: Emit http_request_start metric
    UHC->>Metrics: Start http_request span
    UHC->>Logger: Log request details (method, url, headers)

    %% Rate Limiting Check
    UHC->>RateLimiter: Check rate limit
    RateLimiter->>RateLimiter: Evaluate request rate
    alt Rate limit exceeded
        RateLimiter->>Metrics: Emit rate_limit_exceeded metric
        RateLimiter->>Logger: Log rate limit warning
        RateLimiter-->>UHC: Rate limit error
        UHC->>Metrics: Emit http_request_failed metric
        UHC-->>Client: RateLimitError
    else Rate limit OK
        RateLimiter-->>UHC: Rate limit allowed
    end

    %% Circuit Breaker Check
    UHC->>CircuitBreaker: Check circuit state
    CircuitBreaker->>CircuitBreaker: Evaluate failure rate
    alt Circuit breaker OPEN
        CircuitBreaker->>Metrics: Emit circuit_breaker_open metric
        CircuitBreaker->>Logger: Log circuit breaker open
        CircuitBreaker-->>UHC: Circuit breaker error
        UHC->>Metrics: Emit http_request_failed metric
        UHC-->>Client: CircuitBreakerError
    else Circuit breaker CLOSED/HALF_OPEN
        CircuitBreaker-->>UHC: Circuit breaker allowed
    end

    %% HTTP Request Execution
    UHC->>HTTP: Execute HTTP request
    HTTP->>Metrics: Start http_client span
    HTTP->>Server: Send HTTP request

    %% Server Response Handling
    alt Server returns success (2xx)
        Server-->>HTTP: Success response (2xx)
        HTTP->>Metrics: Emit http_success metric
        HTTP->>CircuitBreaker: Record success
        CircuitBreaker->>CircuitBreaker: Decrease failure rate
        CircuitBreaker->>Metrics: Emit circuit_breaker_success metric
        HTTP-->>UHC: Success response
        UHC->>Logger: Log response details (status, headers)
        UHC->>Metrics: Emit http_request_complete metric
        UHC-->>Client: Response data
    else Server returns client error (4xx)
        Server-->>HTTP: Client error (4xx)
        HTTP->>Metrics: Emit http_client_error metric
        HTTP->>CircuitBreaker: Record failure
        CircuitBreaker->>CircuitBreaker: Increase failure rate
        CircuitBreaker->>Metrics: Emit circuit_breaker_failure metric
        HTTP-->>UHC: Client error response
        
        %% Retry Logic for Client Errors
        UHC->>RetryPolicy: Check retry eligibility
        RetryPolicy->>RetryPolicy: Evaluate error type (429, 408, etc.)
        alt Retry eligible
            RetryPolicy->>Metrics: Emit http_retry metric
            RetryPolicy->>Logger: Log retry attempt
            RetryPolicy->>RetryPolicy: Calculate backoff delay
            RetryPolicy->>RetryPolicy: Wait for backoff
            RetryPolicy-->>UHC: Retry request
            UHC->>HTTP: Retry HTTP request
        else No retry
            RetryPolicy-->>UHC: No retry
            UHC->>Metrics: Emit http_request_failed metric
            UHC-->>Client: HTTPClientError
        end
    else Server returns server error (5xx)
        Server-->>HTTP: Server error (5xx)
        HTTP->>Metrics: Emit http_server_error metric
        HTTP->>CircuitBreaker: Record failure
        CircuitBreaker->>CircuitBreaker: Increase failure rate
        CircuitBreaker->>Metrics: Emit circuit_breaker_failure metric
        HTTP-->>UHC: Server error response
        
        %% Retry Logic for Server Errors
        UHC->>RetryPolicy: Check retry eligibility
        RetryPolicy->>RetryPolicy: Evaluate error type (500, 502, 503, etc.)
        alt Retry eligible
            RetryPolicy->>Metrics: Emit http_retry metric
            RetryPolicy->>Logger: Log retry attempt
            RetryPolicy->>RetryPolicy: Calculate exponential backoff
            RetryPolicy->>RetryPolicy: Wait for backoff
            RetryPolicy-->>UHC: Retry request
            UHC->>HTTP: Retry HTTP request
        else No retry or max retries exceeded
            RetryPolicy-->>UHC: No retry
            UHC->>Metrics: Emit http_request_failed metric
            UHC-->>Client: HTTPServerError
        end
    else Network error
        HTTP->>Metrics: Emit http_network_error metric
        HTTP->>CircuitBreaker: Record failure
        CircuitBreaker->>CircuitBreaker: Increase failure rate
        CircuitBreaker->>Metrics: Emit circuit_breaker_failure metric
        HTTP-->>UHC: Network error
        
        %% Retry Logic for Network Errors
        UHC->>RetryPolicy: Check retry eligibility
        RetryPolicy->>RetryPolicy: Evaluate error type (timeout, connection refused)
        alt Retry eligible
            RetryPolicy->>Metrics: Emit http_retry metric
            RetryPolicy->>Logger: Log retry attempt
            RetryPolicy->>RetryPolicy: Calculate exponential backoff
            RetryPolicy->>RetryPolicy: Wait for backoff
            RetryPolicy-->>UHC: Retry request
            UHC->>HTTP: Retry HTTP request
        else No retry or max retries exceeded
            RetryPolicy-->>UHC: No retry
            UHC->>Metrics: Emit http_request_failed metric
            UHC-->>Client: HTTPNetworkError
        end
    end

    %% Circuit Breaker State Transition
    alt Failure rate exceeds threshold
        CircuitBreaker->>CircuitBreaker: Transition to OPEN state
        CircuitBreaker->>Metrics: Emit circuit_breaker_opened metric
        CircuitBreaker->>Logger: Log circuit breaker opened
    end

    %% Cleanup
    UHC->>Metrics: Finish http_request span
    UHC->>Logger: Log request completion details

    Note over Client, Logger: End of HTTP Request/Response Flow
```

## Key Components

### UnifiedHTTPClient (ADR-032)
- **UnifiedHTTPClient**: Centralized HTTP client with consistent behavior
- **Rate Limiter**: Prevents API rate limit violations
- **Circuit Breaker**: Prevents cascading failures
- **Retry Policy**: Handles transient failures with exponential backoff

### HTTP Client
- **HTTP Client**: Underlying HTTP client implementation
- **External API Server**: Target API endpoint

### Observability
- **Metrics/Tracing**: Comprehensive HTTP request metrics and distributed tracing
- **Structured Logger**: Detailed logging for debugging and monitoring

## Error Handling

### Rate Limiting
- **Rate limit exceeded**: Returns `RateLimitError` immediately
- **Rate limit OK**: Proceeds with request

### Circuit Breaker
- **OPEN state**: Returns `CircuitBreakerError` immediately
- **CLOSED/HALF_OPEN state**: Allows requests with monitoring
- **Failure rate threshold**: Triggers OPEN state when exceeded

### Retry Logic
- **Client errors (4xx)**: Retry for specific codes (429, 408)
- **Server errors (5xx)**: Retry with exponential backoff
- **Network errors**: Retry with exponential backoff
- **Max retries**: Prevents infinite retry loops

## ADR References

- **ADR-032**: Unified HTTP Client — centralized HTTP client implementation
- **ADR-010**: Local-Only Deployment — no external orchestration required
- **ADR-040**: Diagram Governance — diagram metadata and quality standards

## Metrics Emitted

- `http_request_start` — HTTP request initiated
- `http_request_complete` — HTTP request completed successfully
- `http_request_failed` — HTTP request failed
- `http_success` — Successful HTTP response (2xx)
- `http_client_error` — Client error response (4xx)
- `http_server_error` — Server error response (5xx)
- `http_network_error` — Network error
- `http_retry` — HTTP retry attempt
- `rate_limit_exceeded` — Rate limit violation
- `circuit_breaker_open` — Circuit breaker in OPEN state
- `circuit_breaker_opened` — Circuit breaker transitioned to OPEN
- `circuit_breaker_success` — Circuit breaker success recorded
- `circuit_breaker_failure` — Circuit breaker failure recorded
